# Secrets and version control
# These must never enter the build context: .env files can carry live
# credentials, and .git/.github carry full history + workflow files. The
# Dockerfile's COPY . step would otherwise ship them into a public image.
.env
.env.*
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.github

# Rebuilt inside the image — copying a local copy would only shadow the
# fresh install/build and bloat the context.
# node_modules: reinstalled via `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` (Dockerfile)
# dist: regenerated by `npm run build` (Dockerfile)
node_modules
dist

# Local/dev tooling artifacts — never needed at build or run time.
.playwright-mcp
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store

# Repo-internal docs and research notes — not read by any Dockerfile RUN
# step or build script, so excluding them is safe and keeps the image lean.
research-notes
research
CLA.md
README.md

# Backlog/PM tooling — not part of the shipped application.
backlog

# Wrong package manager lockfile — the image installs via pnpm-lock.yaml
# (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`); a stray npm lockfile must not ride
# along in the context.
package-lock.json

# Local database/data files — never shipped in the image; the app expects
# a database to be bind-mounted at /database at runtime.
*.kuzu
*.duckdb
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Local dataset checkout — regenerated inside the image by
# `npm run fetch-datasets` (FetchDatasets.js), so a locally-fetched copy
# is redundant and safe to exclude. NOTE: datasets.json (the fetch config)
# is NOT excluded — FetchDatasets.js reads it at build time.
datasets

# Uninitialized/dev-only kuzu submodule checkout. The Dockerfile builds
# against the "kuzu" npm package (installed via pnpm into node_modules/kuzu)
# and reads grammar sources from node_modules/kuzu/kuzu-source — it never
# references the top-level kuzu/ submodule. That path is only used by the
# dev-only `build-kuzu`/`generate-grammar` npm scripts, not by the
# Dockerfile's `generate-grammar-prod` step.
kuzu
